{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"prompt\": \"Minecraft builder reference sheet for a Roman villa, vanilla Minecraft blocks only, crisp voxel style, plain light background, no characters or animals. Landscape canvas about 3:2. Exactly two views side by side: LEFT straight-on front elevation, orthographic; RIGHT elevated three-quarter view at the same block scale, showing the courts through their open roofs. Both depict the same complete building. Skilled human builder quality: real low, long massing, depth with projecting details and recessed framed openings, real roof verges, eaves and ridges, precise stairs, slabs, trapdoors, bars and lantern details. Overall footprint 36 blocks wide by 48 deep, 10 tall, roof ridges at height 9. Do not enlarge the building or make it a palace.\\nSite: street-facing symmetrical cream plaster front with red painted dado at base. Terracotta-colored tile roofs slope inward toward the courts. Central recessed fauces doorway with pediment made of white quartz stairs and two bronze-looking lantern lamps on quartz posts. Exactly four shuttered shop rooms flank it, two per side, dark oak shutters open on quartz counters. Stone-paved approach in front. Behind doorway an atrium open to sky through a square roof opening, shallow water rain pool beneath, black and white mosaic floor with red accents, a potted plant at each side, tablinum facing entrance across atrium. Behind that a peristyle garden: white quartz columns with slab capitals ring a grass court, low green hedges frame two planted beds with rose bushes and flowers, rectilinear square fountain basin (no curved or round geometry) of quartz slabs with water jet on central quartz column, two bronze-green block-built statues on andesite plinths among beds. Dining room with couches on three sides, bedrooms and kitchen hearth off courts; show only what is naturally visible through open courts, do not remove front walls for a cutaway.\\nExact permitted Minecraft block ids by role:\\nwalls: smooth_quartz\\ndado: red_terracotta\\ncolumns: quartz_pillar, quartz_slab\\nplinth: polished_andesite, polished_andesite_slab\\nmosaic: white_terracotta, black_terracotta, red_terracotta\\ncourt: grass_block\\npaths: smooth_stone, smooth_stone_slab\\nhedges: azalea_leaves\\nflowers: rose_bush, cornflower, poppy\\nfountain: smooth_quartz_slab, quartz_block, water\\nstatue: oxidized_copper, oxidized_cut_copper_slab\\ndoors: dark_oak_door\\nshutters: dark_oak_trapdoor\\nwindows: iron_bars\\nlamps: lantern, quartz_pillar\\npots: potted_fern, potted_azalea_bush\\nroof_field: bricks, red_nether_bricks, brick_stairs, red_nether_brick_stairs, brick_slab, red_nether_brick_slab\\nroof_eave: bricks\\nroof_ridge: quartz_slab\\nroof_verge: quartz_block\\npediment: quartz_stairs\\ncouch_frame: dark_oak_stairs\\ncouch_cushion: red_carpet\\ntable: dark_oak_slab\\nhearth: campfire, stone_bricks\\nkitchen: smoker, stone_bricks\\nstorage: barrel\\nbeds: red_bed\\ncounters: smooth_quartz\\nAdditional permitted functional/decor blocks: bookshelf, lectern, barrel, lantern, quartz_pillar, flower_pot, potted_fern, potted_azalea_bush, red_carpet, red_bed, dark_oak_slab, dark_oak_stairs, campfire, smoker, stone_bricks.\\nUse actual Minecraft block shapes and textures. No smooth nonvoxel architectural curves, no invented blocks, no additional materials. Minimal labels FRONT ELEVATION and THREE-QUARTER VIEW, no palette legend.\",\n  \"roles\": [\n    {\"role\":\"walls\",\"blocks\":[\"smooth_quartz\"]},\n    {\"role\":\"dado\",\"blocks\":[\"red_terracotta\"]},\n    {\"role\":\"columns\",\"blocks\":[\"quartz_pillar\",\"quartz_slab\",\"quartz_stairs\",\"quartz_block\"]},\n    {\"role\":\"plinth\",\"blocks\":[\"polished_andesite\",\"polished_andesite_slab\"]},\n    {\"role\":\"mosaic\",\"blocks\":[\"white_terracotta\",\"black_terracotta\",\"red_terracotta\"]},\n    {\"role\":\"court\",\"blocks\":[\"grass_block\"]},\n    {\"role\":\"paths\",\"blo